From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:00:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Per player fog of war

Lets plugins turn fog of war on or off per viewer with Player#setFogOfWar, falling back to fogOfWar.default in cubing.yml. A server with modes in one shared world sets fogOfWar.default to false and enables it for the players of the modes that want it.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
index 59fa188c..81d953c4 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
@@ -1391,4 +1391,23 @@ public interface Player extends HumanEntity, Conversable, CommandSender, Offline
 
     Spigot spigot();
     // Spigot end
+
+    // CubingPaper start - Per player fog of war
+    /**
+     * Gets whether fog of war applies to this player as a viewer, so players it could not see are not sent to it.
+     * Always false while fog of war is disabled in cubing.yml.
+     *
+     * @return whether fog of war applies to this player
+     */
+    boolean hasFogOfWar();
+
+    /**
+     * Sets whether fog of war applies to this player as a viewer, overriding fogOfWar.default in cubing.yml.
+     * Has no effect while fog of war is disabled in cubing.yml. Takes effect at the next check, within
+     * fogOfWar.interval-ticks. Main thread only.
+     *
+     * @param enabled true or false to override, or null to use fogOfWar.default
+     */
+    void setFogOfWar(Boolean enabled);
+    // CubingPaper end
 }
